{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PuJAyQS13CzYAL9N61","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K8nZxFWXyG5AetaPPFgqUU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"Output dirs\n(`test-results`, `playwright-report`) are gitignored.\n\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"Outside CI the config reuses any server already on port 8899, which\nmay be a sibling worktree's older build; if only new tests fail, check\n`lsof -i :8899` and re-run. To watch hydration, start a\n`MutationObserver` from `addInitScript` at `readystatechange` ->\n`interactive` (before the module script runs) and push records in the\ncallback: delivered records are gone, so `takeRecords()` alone reads\nnothing.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 11: example page visible without JS, quiet under hydration\n\n## Done\n1. e2e (test/e2e/hydration.spec.ts): three new tests, all red first.\n   - \"the page is visible when no script loads\": .js aborted, computed\n     opacity of <html> != 0 on /.\n   - \"hydrating /list replaces no text inside badges\" and \"... writes\n     no attributes\": MutationObserver started from addInitScript at\n     readystatechange=interactive, records pushed in the callback.\n     Red causes: Badge setup rewrote textContent; reveal removed the\n     html class (attribute write).\n2. Deleted reduce-fouce (index.html class + noscript, index.css rule),\n   client/util.ts (reveal) and its call, the reveal unit tests in\n   test/index.ts, and the test:hydration test that asserted the class\n   was present (the behaviour is removed, not weakened). Dropped the\n   obsolete `not.toHaveClass(/reduce-fouce/)` lines in e2e.\n3. Badge setup writes text only if `textContent !== label`.\n4. client/index.ts imports Badge, Notice, then Counter, with a comment.\n   No test added: order is config. The existing runtime assertion\n   (Counter.render undefined) and its e2e check still pass. I could not\n   find an observable failure from the old order to test against.\n5. README: util.ts entry replaced, index.ts entry notes the order,\n   badge entry describes write-on-change, cascade paragraph explains\n   evaluation order. toc:hydration re-run (no TOC change).\n\n## Gotchas\n- takeRecords() after a no-op callback returns nothing: records were\n  already delivered. Accumulate in the callback.\n- One e2e run had exactly the three new tests fail, then 8+ clean runs.\n  Likely a sibling worktree's server on 8899 (reuseExistingServer).\n- Delete example-hydration/build before lint; test:hydration needs\n  `npm run build` (dist/htm.js) first.\n\n## Verified\ntest:e2e 15/15, test:hydration 112 + 17, lint, typecheck, npm test 410.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git reset -q .nightralph && git commit -qm \"AGENTS: e2e port reuse and hydration observer notes; lint fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short && git log --oneline -4"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":79415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9beed691-8607-45ea-9b6a-1ec3943819d3","uuid":"4033c20c-5ebe-4895-af48-577bfbab99e9","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:31:34.888Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3PuHsNPFETcDn91STps","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01K8nZxFWXyG5AetaPPFgqUU":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"Output dirs\n(`test-results`, `playwright-report`) are gitignored.\n\"\"\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"Outside CI the config reuses any server already on port 8899, which\nmay be a sibling worktree's older build; if only new tests fail, check\n`lsof -i :8899` and re-run. To watch hydration, start a\n`MutationObserver` from `addInitScript` at `readystatechange` ->\n`interactive` (before the module script runs) and push records in the\ncallback: delivered records are gone, so `takeRecords()` alone reads\nnothing.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nmkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 11: example page visible without JS, quiet under hydration\n\n## Done\n1. e2e (test/e2e/hydration.spec.ts): three new tests, all red first.\n   - \"the page is visible when no script loads\": .js aborted, computed\n     opacity of <html> != 0 on /.\n   - \"hydrating /list replaces no text inside badges\" and \"... writes\n     no attributes\": MutationObserver started from addInitScript at\n     readystatechange=interactive, records pushed in the callback.\n     Red causes: Badge setup rewrote textContent; reveal removed the\n     html class (attribute write).\n2. Deleted reduce-fouce (index.html class + noscript, index.css rule),\n   client/util.ts (reveal) and its call, the reveal unit tests in\n   test/index.ts, and the test:hydration test that asserted the class\n   was present (the behaviour is removed, not weakened). Dropped the\n   obsolete `not.toHaveClass(/reduce-fouce/)` lines in e2e.\n3. Badge setup writes text only if `textContent !== label`.\n4. client/index.ts imports Badge, Notice, then Counter, with a comment.\n   No test added: order is config. The existing runtime assertion\n   (Counter.render undefined) and its e2e check still pass. I could not\n   find an observable failure from the old order to test against.\n5. README: util.ts entry replaced, index.ts entry notes the order,\n   badge entry describes write-on-change, cascade paragraph explains\n   evaluation order. toc:hydration re-run (no TOC change).\n\n## Gotchas\n- takeRecords() after a no-op callback returns nothing: records were\n  already delivered. Accumulate in the callback.\n- One e2e run had exactly the three new tests fail, then 8+ clean runs.\n  Likely a sibling worktree's server on 8899 (reuseExistingServer).\n- Delete example-hydration/build before lint; test:hydration needs\n  `npm run build` (dist/htm.js) first.\n\n## Verified\ntest:e2e 15/15, test:hydration 112 + 17, lint, typecheck, npm test 410.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git reset -q .nightralph && git commit -qm \"AGENTS: e2e port reuse and hydration observer notes; lint fix\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short && git log --oneline -4"}}}
