{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3PvSquZHZPTtvG1mBAZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] With every `.js` request aborted, the document's computed opacity is not 0 after load on `/`\n[x] On `/list`, a MutationObserver started at `interactive` sees no text node replacement inside badge hosts during hydration\n[x] On `/list`, the same observer sees no attribute mutations during hydration\n[x] The client entry's import order places Badge and Notice before Counter, and the stripped client still asserts Counter has no render\n[x] `npm run test:e2e`, `npm run test:hydration` and `npm run lint` pass\n\nTicket 11 is done: the example page now shows without JavaScript, and hydrating `/list` changes nothing in the DOM. All of it is in three commits.\n\n**Tests first.** I added three Playwright tests in `test/e2e/hydration.spec.ts`, and each failed before the fix for the expected reason:\n- **No JS:** with every `.js` request blocked, the page's opacity on `/` is not 0. It was 0 before.\n- **Badge text:** on `/list`, an observer started at `interactive` sees no text replaced inside badges. Before, Badge's setup rewrote its text on every load.\n- **Attributes:** the same observer sees no attribute writes. The only one before was the `reduce-fouce` class being removed from `<html>`.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- **Opacity gate gone:** the `reduce-fouce` class, its `<noscript>` override and its CSS rule are deleted. `client/util.ts` (`reveal`) and the call to it are deleted too.\n- **Badge:** its setup now writes the label only when it differs from the text already there.\n- **Import order:** `client/index.ts` imports Badge and Notice before Counter, with a comment explaining why. The runtime check that Counter has no render is still there.\n\n**Tests removed.** I deleted tests for behaviour that no longer exists: the two `reveal` unit tests in `test/index.ts`, the hydration test that required the class on the scaffold, and the `not.toHaveClass(/reduce-fouce/)` lines in the e2e file.\n\n**Not tested.** The import order has no test of its own. I couldn't find anything observable that breaks with the old order, so I treated it as config and recorded that in the notes.\n\n**Docs:**\n- **README:** it no longer mentions `util.ts`. It now describes the \"write only when it differs\" pattern for any setup that writes server-rendered content, and explains how cascade changes the order modules run in. `toc:hydration` was re-run.\n- **AGENTS.md:** two notes for future work. Outside CI, Playwright reuses whatever server is already on port 8899, so a sibling worktree's older build can answer. And a MutationObserver has to collect records in its callback, because `takeRecords()` only returns ones not yet delivered.\n\n**Results:** `test:e2e` passes 15/15. One run failed only the three new tests together; the next eight runs were clean. My best guess is a sibling worktree's server on 8899, but I didn't confirm it. `test:hydration` (112 + 17), `lint`, `typecheck` and `npm test` (410) all pass. I deleted the build folder afterwards, and nothing is left listening on ports 8899 or 8123."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129,"cache_read_input_tokens":81220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9beed691-8607-45ea-9b6a-1ec3943819d3","uuid":"ba8e012c-2a12-462e-ad52-81d78378fd17","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:31:50.950Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3PvS9ykSi59egeAF97j"}
